case timeline-frcp-served
uses frcp-civil-procedure ^2024.12.0
as_of 2024-12-20
summary "Timeline fixture: frcp-filed with the service its first world assumes recorded, dated before the service period's due date."
notes "Test fixture for `litigate timeline` (lg-z2m.1): the child of `frcp-filed`, which inserts a triggering event (ProcessServed, which starts the answer period) ahead of the parent's service-period row. Every key the parent has stays identical. The dates are illustrative, not a real matter's."
start frcp-civil-procedure::service-window
perspective plaintiff

parties {
  plaintiff: applicant Corporation
}

events {
  2024-12-02 ComplaintFiled() by plaintiff
  2024-12-10 ProcessServed() on plaintiff
}

stakes { frcp-civil-procedure::rule41d-costs-ordered: 0.usd, frcp-civil-procedure::refiling-proceeds: 0.usd, frcp-civil-procedure::dismissal-fees-eligible: 0.usd, frcp-civil-procedure::dismissal-fees-ineligible: 0.usd }
